From 67023198eee8d130abc4f64f97d0bb4f05956aab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: noble6 <ruanproject01@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:12:24 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] renderengine: Add the Strand blur filter

Dual filter Kawase blur with the same look as KawaseBlurDualFilterV2
(same shaders and radius mapping) that skips work it has already done.

Backdrop cache: SkiaRenderEngine now tells the blur filter which layers
were drawn below the blurred one. When those layers and the display
settings match an earlier frame, the input pixels match too, so:
 - same rect and radius: the previous result is returned, no GPU work
 - same rect, new radius: the downsample pyramid is kept and only the
   upsample passes run

This is the notification shade over a still launcher or app: the shade
content scrolls and animates, the blurred backdrop doesn't. Layers that
can change pixels without changing their settings (front buffered,
command stream) turn the cache off for that frame.

Every pass renders to surfaces kept by the filter, 8-bit and opaque
unless the input is F16, and discards the old contents when it
overwrites them. Upsample targets are separate from the pyramid.

sys.strand.blur.lite=1 caps the passes at two for battery and thermal
profiles. ro.strand.blur.cache=false turns the cache off.

Strand is the default; debug.renderengine.blur_algorithm=kawase2 selects
KawaseBlurDualFilterV2 again.
